# Code style

## Always brace `if` bodies

Never put an `if` body on the same line without braces. Always use `{ }`, with the body on its own line. This applies to `else`, `for`, and `while` too.

```ts
// Bad
if (!text || sending) return;

// Good
if (!text || sending) {
  return;
}
```

## Separate conceptually distinct blocks with a blank line

Put a blank line between groups of statements that do different things, for example: input validation, setting up state, the main work, and building the result. Keep statements that belong to one step together, without blank lines between them.

```ts
// Bad
const text = content.trim();
if (!text) {
  return;
}
const started = performance.now();
setSending(true);
const response = await fetch("/api/chat", { method: "POST", body });

// Good
const text = content.trim();
if (!text) {
  return;
}

const started = performance.now();
setSending(true);

const response = await fetch("/api/chat", { method: "POST", body });
```
